Enlarge the board to 90x90 mm for hand routing

With 3.5 mm between footprints the board grows to 90x90 mm, which leaves
wide corridors for manual routing. Placement, mounting holes and the GND
plane are unchanged and DRC stays at 0 violations with 63 unrouted items.

An A* autorouter (2 layers, vias, exact geometric validation, per-net
rollback) was implemented and evaluated at 75, 90 and 160 mm. It only ever
routed 1-6 of the 29 nets before deadlocking: when several adjacent pads of
a connector need to escape, the first track occupies the corridor the next
one needs, and without rip-up-and-retry there is no way out. The code was
removed rather than left in the tree as broken tooling; DESIGN.md records
the finding so it is not attempted again blindly.

